PatternFly 6 theme for OpenStack Horizon
========================================

  patternfly: 6.7.0
  source:     https://www.npmjs.com/package/@patternfly/patternfly (tarball
              https://registry.npmjs.org/@patternfly/patternfly/-/patternfly-6.7.0.tgz)
  vendored:   2026-10-26
  license:    MIT (PatternFly), SIL OFL 1.1 (Red Hat Text/Display/Mono fonts),
              CC-BY-4.0 (PatternFly icons)

Files vendored from the npm tarball, byte for byte:

  patternfly-base-no-globals.css   <- package/patternfly-base-no-globals.css
  patternfly-charts.css            <- package/patternfly-charts.css
  assets/fonts/RedHatText/*.woff2
  assets/fonts/RedHatDisplay/*.woff2
  assets/fonts/RedHatMono/*.woff2
  assets/fonts/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2
  assets/pficon/pf-v6-pficon.woff2
  assets/images/{Felt,PF}-Bkg-Generic-{Light,Dark}.svg

Deliberately NOT vendored: patternfly.css / patternfly.min.css (the ~1.8 MB
component stylesheet). Horizon renders Bootstrap 3 markup; shipping PF component
CSS would only add ~1.5 MB of rules that never match and would fight Bootstrap's
own component styles. Only the token + font + reset layer and the chart colour
tokens are needed. See docs/ASSETS.md for how to add components later.

No file in this directory has been modified. Do not hand-edit them: update by
re-running the procedure in docs/ASSETS.md so the checksums stay meaningful.
